WEBVTT

00:00:56.573 --> 00:01:00.590
he has a talent for synthesizing
ideas from different fields --

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:04.804
sociology, history, psychology,
politics and economics --

00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:08.476
and then weaving them
into clarifying insights

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.515
highly relevant to where we are today.

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:13.066
David recently published

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.260
"The Second Mountain:
The Quest for a Moral Life."

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:19.703
It’s a book anchored in his own
search for meaning,

00:01:19.727 --> 00:01:21.902
following a divorce six years ago.

00:01:21.926 --> 00:01:25.346
And in his TED Talk In April,
he made the case

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:29.839
that the key to us finding a better way
forward in our divided politics

00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:35.180
is to focus on deeper human values
and the rich connections between us.